3. Commercial Offerings require permission

Without the Licensor's prior explicit written permission, you may not make
the Software, a modified version, or its functionality available to others
as a Commercial Offering. This includes:

  a. Selling, licensing, renting or otherwise charging for copies or access.
  b. Offering it as a paid or subscription-based hosted service.
  c. Including it as a component or feature of a paid product, service,
     membership or bundle, even if you describe that component as free.
  d. Monetizing access to it or its functionality through advertising,
     sponsorship or other consideration tied to providing the Software.

These restrictions apply equally to original, modified, forked, rebranded and
embedded versions. Providing the Software free of charge is permitted when
it is not a Commercial Offering. Voluntary donations that are not required
for access or functionality do not by themselves make it a Commercial Offering.

Charging for work you create or edit using the Software is permitted. Using
Retouch as an internal tool for a business or to deliver client work does not
by itself make that work a Commercial Offering of Retouch.

